# sqlx hashes each migration file byte-for-byte and refuses to run
# (VersionMismatch) if an already-applied migration's checksum no longer
# matches what was recorded in `_sqlx_migrations`. Without this, Windows
# checkouts can silently flip these files between LF and CRLF depending on
# core.autocrlf and checkout history, corrupting the recorded checksum and
# permanently disabling the local database. Pin them to LF so the bytes never
# drift across platforms or checkouts.
src-tauri/migrations/*.sql text eol=lf
